! Write a function to find the roots of a quartic equation, that is solve
! the equation ax⁴ + bx³ + cx² + dx + e = 0.
! 
! This equation has a solution in closed form. Your program must handle
! complex, real and duplicate roots. Input checking and error display is
! optional.
! 
! The internet shows many, many quartic equation solvers and algorithms. A
! few examples.
! 
! Wikipedia Very extensive article, including several algorithms.
! 
! 1728.org Step-by-step solution with examples and a calculator.
! 
! Wolfram Mathworld No examples.
! 
! PlanetCalc No step-by-step, but with a calculator.
! 
! Whatever algorithm you choose, it's very likely you'll need:
! 
! Arithmetic/Complex
! 
! Roots of a quadratic function
! 
! Roots of a cubic polynomial


